  ('zcrm_1579374000076262009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000053678052', 'Dennis Bakken', NULL, 'Dennis called in regarding a colonoscopy from 2019 that he just recently received a bill for in the mail. Dennis is wondering why this was not paid as he thought it had been paid in 2019. It appears there were some diagnostic pathology biopsies done during this colonoscopy and I explained to Dennis that once a test becomes diagnostic, it is an out of pocket expense. I also explained to Dennis how his IUA worked in 2019 and how it currently works. Dennis does not understand this concept and is requesting that he is sent a letter stating that his MEC (RCI) would not pay for his preventative (that became diagnostic due to pathology tests) colonoscopy so that Sedera will pay it for him. I explained that this is not how the plans work and that he will have to pay the $418.00 out of pocket for this test. Hopefully my 3rd attempt at explaining this to Dennis will take, he just does not seem to understand the plan he had or the plan he currently has with MPB. -JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-09-27 07:23:37', '2021-09-27 07:23:37'),
