  ('zcrm_1579374000075700018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025439119', 'Steven Arck', NULL, 'Rose called.  Steven is aging into  Medicare 10/1/21.  Sent Rose the template w/cancellation link &amp; Patti''s info.  She also LM for Patti so she''ll know to expect &amp; look for the request since timing is so close.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-09-16 16:24:49', '2021-09-16 16:24:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000075700013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031672299', 'Melissa Lagassie', NULL, 'Melissa called very frustrated that we had not paid her bill.  With some conversation, it sounds like the APEX preventative card she presented (& was billed) was probably declined because it moved into diagnostic with polyp(s) removed.  Multiple times we went over we do not receive, pay, or see the bills sent to the various entities involved in her plan.  She says this is ridiculous and is very upset.  I let her know it''s a simple shift in direction and sent her the template for how to submit a need to Sedera.  That once she starts the need, she should be able to talk with her need advisor and get this straightened out.  Not really sure she was any happier at the end.  I feel like I really tried to let her know it''s going to be okay we just need to shift our mindset and where it''s billed.  We did discuss that moving into diagnostic, she will have the $500 IUA.    CA

Melissa called back -- now even more frustrated:  "It''s beyond frustrating that I''ve spent three hours of my evening" and you should be able to help me...  She says she''s gotten help with billing before and we could see everything, so why can''t I?  Sedera told her I should be able to see all the things we''d been billed for.  I told her it''s my understanding the billing does not come to us, but goes to each separate entity in the plan (ie: APEX, Sedera, etc.).  However, since I''m the evening and newer concierge person, maybe I am unaware of how I can see everything.  That I would send Kelly Anne a chat so she & Jennifer can 1) touch base with Melissa & help her  2) train me on how to see the bills so I can learn.  Included Melissa''s wk #: 860-953-4884, where she''ll be tomorrow.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-09-16 16:02:14', '2021-09-16 18:09:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000075700008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060779416', 'Christine Heinritz', NULL, 'tt Christine, she''s ready to submit the invoices for her rotator cuff (I think that''s what she said) injury,  Sent her the template for submitting a need to Zion.  She thinks she''s over the $2500 IUA.   We went over what to tell the surgeon (who is watching the situation & trying alt to surgery for now) and physical therapist.  Discussed if surgery is req''d to contact concierge w/plenty of time & we may be able to help = benefit for her because then they consider reducing the IUA on the need, as well as how IUA works on a need (ie: not annual).    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-09-16 15:40:01', '2021-09-16 15:40:01'),
