  ('zcrm_1579374000075455003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073951215', 'Gayle Johnson', NULL, 'I got a list of ophthalmologist''s and a fair price for a visit and emailed it to Gayle.  I let her know that vision was not a covered expense, it would need to be medical for Zion to share in it.  She understood, she is afraid that she looked at the sun too long. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-09-14 07:31:36', '2021-09-14 07:31:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000075441013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000075811278', 'Sheri Bowes', NULL, 'tt Sheri.  She curr has Liberty &amp; is very sure she knows how this all works, yet in discussing how the IUAs work was completely off.  Difficult to get her to slow down and discuss.  Asked about pre-x: she says only person is husb who is diabetic &amp; has high bp = both well maintained &amp; it''s been 10-years on those 2 items since he''s been in the hosp.  Sent her e-mail w/Zion''s Memb Guidelines, deadline for Oct 1st eff date, and more info.  Not sure who referred her so for now put she visited our website.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-09-13 17:44:47', '2021-09-13 17:44:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000075433008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081054002', 'Stephanie Foo', NULL, '9-13-21 Stephanie and Joey are both 33 and both self-employed. Stephanie is not a good candidate and will keep ins. She has chronic acid reflux, requires endoscopy every few years, has endometriosis and requires some treatment and an ultrasound every year. She also finally revealed after a long time that she has a currently dislocated shoulder and a hand injury as well! She can''t go to the doctors she wants because they are all out of network, hence their desire to switch. They have a $2200 month plan with BC/BS!  They like the idea of the HSA.  Joey may be able to join. He has ulcerative colitis and needs a colonoscopy 1x per year. Takes some expensive meds also. He has VA plan also! He''s going to inquire if he can get his colonscopy and meds from the VA which would then make this a viable option. "This product is US only so we won''t be any help.  Apriso 375mg x 120tabs $553.09 + $4.95.  Mesalamine Supp 1gm x 90supps $324.32 + $9.95 shipping." Mesalamine is for 3 months and Apriso is only for 1 month. He also takes prednesone for $4-$5 and celebrex for $10-$11. Celebrex might be for Stephanie. I forget. They also need dental work. Joey needs implants. Stephanie is interested in maternity, both of which is perfect use of HMA. I talked about the $140 HMA giving them access to $10,000 for all of these other costs they will incur and they can use it with traditional ins also, which made Stephanie happy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-09-13 15:04:26', '2021-09-13 15:06:37'),
