Luther Setzer', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-09-03 09:07:08', '2021-09-03 09:07:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074936003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071712116', 'Dorcas Mella', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2021-09-03 08:31:46', '2021-09-03 08:31:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074919003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071780031', 'Kora Gilbert', NULL, 'Drew and Kora called for an explanation of their preventative care benefits- I went over everything, found their pediatrician in the PHCS network, told them that they need to confirm with the provider that they are currently participating in the PHCS network and send both preventative care emails. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-09-03 07:51:32', '2021-09-03 07:51:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074903003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058023086', 'Lisa Schuster', NULL, 'Member submitted Member Change form to add newborn son to membership.  I will notify Zion &amp; let her know to get us the SS#.  No change in pricing', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-09-03 07:40:12', '2021-09-03 07:40:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074886003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000191450', 'Terese McGroarty', NULL, 'Teresa called.  Her husband Mark ended-up in the ER &amp; hospital earlier this week and was diagnosed with diabetes (hasn''t had this before, so not pre-x).  Sent her the template on submitting a need to Zion, went over IUA of 5k, and let her know I''d get answers for her tomorrow on any options we might have in helping them get insulin.   (They think he''ll eventually be able to come off the  insuling.)    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-09-02 17:55:30', '2021-09-02 17:56:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074882011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078309004', 'James Skurski', NULL, '9-2-21 Jim is 53 wife is 54. Wife is healthy, no pre-x. Both no tobacco. Jim  had a hip replacement on March 16, 2021. PT ended in June. But, he is currently doing PT for his knee from a surgery he had done back in 2015. PT may take 2-3 months now to avoid future problems. He doesn''t foresee any surgery. This should solve the problem. Also did a colonoscopy which was normal. But, he has some GI issues and has EE (inflammation of the esophagus) which he takes meds for. He periodically has scope done and did one end of July 2021. They''re on Cobra now but got laid off in May, 2020. Therefore, they need Nov. 1st start date. He''s happy that through ASHI is the $100 waived enrollment fee. Looking at SECURE for both or just wife, $1000/$500. He already has an HSA and happy to keep funding it and use it for PT if need be. I will connect him with Darius to run traditional ins quote. He wants to explore all options. He will share it all with his wife.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-09-02 17:07:29', '2021-09-15 13:24:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000074882003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810847', 'Sally Hammond', NULL, '9-2-21 Sally and Pete are curious about SECURE. Both are self-employed. Pete is the only one with possible pre-x which they will determine better very soon. He had gall bladder surgery 1 year ago. He recently had a colonoscopy and scope and they found nothing on the biopsy. He will ask doctor togive him a clean bill of health if possible. Sally really only goes for annual wellness visits and nothing else. But, both have been seeing chiro for maintenance/wellness. Sally just had discomfort in back which they have resolved. But, she still like to go, especially since it was included in membership with Redirect. She understands they will lose that and pay the $65 cash price. But, also understands whatever she''s been seeing chiro for will be considered pre-x. She will discuss with Pete. They don''t want to unnecessarily expose themselves to risk. I gave them all risks of pre-x clause. She knows of the 20th deadline and will let me know.  Also Pete sees PCP for random injuries from time to time which they will have to pay for or use app moving forward. She understands and says it''s about $250 which is still better than paying PDHC $970/$1000 vs SECURE $500/$1000.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-09-02 15:39:54', '2021-09-02 15:42:37');
