  ('zcrm_1579374000073889003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034713014', 'Joseph Sands', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation form since he will be turning 65.  I will notify Sedera &amp; RCI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-08-19 06:55:25', '2021-08-19 06:55:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073874016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041271176', 'Ted Williams', NULL, 'Ted called back.  Juan, the advisor he talked to at Sedera was really harsh with him.  (He must have asked to speak to someone else, because he said the Sedera guy said he was the only one there & there was no one else to talk with.)   The member said the guy went totally by script & was hard to work with.  45-minutes later, he did have a need setup.  He''ll receive an e-mail next week from his need advisor. 

BUT, they will NOT do this via mail (mail''s not reliable, they don''t want your info out there, etc.).  So, he''s quite frustrated.  He''s thinking he''s now going to have to go buy a scanner!  All his bills come to him via US Mail, so he must scan them to upload them.  I saw a flyer on Sedera''s site yesterday for submitting things via an app on his smart phone but cannot find it again even after 1/2 hour of looking.   

The Sedera guy scolded him about how non-life threatening things must have a second opinion!  Yet, he''s had so much liquid around his lungs (14 liters in the last 2 weeks-ish) it''s been life threatening & each procedure''s been to help keep him breathing.  I did find info on second opinions in the blog so sent him that for his reference.  

He sounds downtrodden!  Here he is having trouble breathing and they guys saying it''s not life threatening!    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-08-18 17:48:23', '2021-08-18 18:38:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073874008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048514133', 'Kelly Fleites', NULL, 'Kelly called.  She''s looking to get her orthotics paid for, but does not have a need for her scoliosis and it doesn''t sound like they''re super expensive.  Then she said something that rang a bell w/this advisor''s members:  "I thought this would pay for all my medical needs."  I''ve experienced Jonathan having a lot of members who also have HMAs, but they think it''s all one product.  So, I let her know Jonathan may have information for her, but I''m thinking it''s a separate product.  She''s going to touch base with him.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-08-18 17:26:02', '2021-08-18 17:26:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000073874003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041271176', 'Ted Williams', NULL, 'Talked w/Ted.  I''d talked with Denny Watkins who works w/Sedera &amp; he gave me manual instructions, so I gave those to Ted.  Then gave Ted Sedera''s # &amp; transferred Ted to Sedera (although, it''s past 5pm) so he can verbally setup his need.  He has surgery tomorrow and another treatment Friday, but will call if he needs anything.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-08-18 16:24:01', '2021-08-18 16:24:01'),
