  ('zcrm_1579374000073854027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006727', 'Charles Korb III', NULL, '8-18-21 A bit challenging to help him understand why his cost will be going from $378 to $578 when he turns 60. He did have a stomach bleed recently on Feb. 15th. He''s not familiar with the value of Redirect and does not have the app on his phone. I sent him the overview and supporting docs of his membership again. He calculated his total monthly cost times number of months he''s been a member and saying MPB is way ahead of the game with what he''s spent vs his one need. His need only cost $2794.85 in total and he paid $500. He''s thinking maybe he should just do this on his own. I shared the cost of traditional ins with him as well. He''s not earning any income and hasn''t for 7 years. So, he qualifies for Medicaid but he''s not sure he wants that. He was hoping he''d get some subsidy bc someone he knows is paying $300+ in FL for medical, dental, vision, etc. I told him none of these include dental or vision. That''s separate. Our Concierge Team wasn''t super helpful when he needed help with Redirect. I''m hesitant to move him to CARE+ since he has this stomach issue that they never really diagnosed. They put him on Prilosec and he''s been fine ever since. But, still risky! Also he would no longer get his annual wellness or any of the benefits from Redirect. He''s only eligible for CARE+ without any income sources. He''ll contact me when he reviews everything further. He understands he can''t join C4 now until Nov. for Jan. 1st.  He was very appreciative by the end and thanked me for all of my help!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-18 13:36:19', '2021-08-18 13:37:09'),
