  ('zcrm_1579374000072972023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073002142', 'Leonard Ott', NULL, '8-4-21 Christopher is 60 and husband is 56. Both healthy, only Christopher is pre diabetic with occasional metformin depending on diet. They are business owners and Christopher just quit his other job which is how they got their ins which ends Aug. 31st. They both just completed their annual wellness visits and all checked out very well. Also Christopher had the cleanest colonoscopy results his doc has seen! Looking at SECURE knowing network is small and Dr. Anne Gaff is not in the network. Possibly choose CARE+ because of this.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-04 17:24:28', '2021-08-04 17:24:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072972018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077374092', 'Dave Owens', NULL, '8-4-21 Dave asked me to call his wife Blaire to answer her final questions and then they are ready to go. I just left Blaire a vm now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-04 15:58:01', '2021-08-04 15:58:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072972013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447234', 'Thomas McCarthy', NULL, '8-3-21 Hi Wendy,
I need your help... Can you please read the email below from Zion Health and call me at your earliest convenience? My wife went to a dermatologist at the request of our MDVIP Primary Care Doctor for two concerns. Fortunately, she found out "early" that she had cancer and the lesions were removed successfully and she is now cancer free.
I submitted a Zion Health "NEED" for this dermatological issue and Zion Health is now attempting to devise a NEED response indicating that two needs must be submitted, one for each skin cancer lesion although they were discovered at the same time. This is not right. They are wanting two needs for two IUA of $1,000 each when both lesions were discovered at the same time. This is not ethically right and I wish to contest this NEEDS outcome finding.
I''ve worked in the healthcare industry for over 33 years and many of my physician colleagues including General Practitioners, Cardiologists, Dermatologists, Orthopedic Surgeons and the like would not separate one claim into two claims in the midst of a treatment plan. The only reason both lesion removal surgeries were not done same day as per the physician recommendation.
Simply stated, Zion Health should not be demanding that one need be split into two needs when the diagnosis was determined on the same day, same appointment and by the same dermatologist. Please help me with this situation. Thanks very much.
My best,
Thomas McCarthy
985-778-1822 CELL

Answer:

Thanks Wendy for forwarding this.

Skin cancers like these usually occur in skin that has been damaged by the sun at some time in the past, probably in teenage years.  They can and do develop anywhere in these areas of damage. Because of this, when a skin cancer is removed, the patient is not cured of skin cancer. Only the area where the cancer was has been “cured”, and once a patient develops a skin cancer, they will develop another in another area at some future time. Each individual cancer has its own “cure”; thus, Zion Health deems each skin cancer as a separate need with a separate IUA, even when more than one is removed during the same visit.

We will be sending this explanation to Tom. Please let me know if you have questions about this.

Jeff', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-04 15:32:50', '2021-08-04 15:32:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072984003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068994027', 'Linda Garcia', NULL, 'Linda called to ask if there was anything else that she or her husband needed to do on their end for their membership. She said she got her Zion health cards and QR Life Code cards, along with having their Welcome Call. So I let her know that they are all set on their end. Linda lastly asked about prescriptions. I explained the whole process to her about the Prescription Quote form and the coupons for low cost''s that we send. The very last thing we discussed was CirrusMD. I checked and made sure both her and her husband are registered and they are, then explained that CirrusMD is the preferred way to go first thing before running to the actual doctor. It can save a lot of time and money. She loves the idea and that is what they will be doing anytime needed. She was ever so thankful for everything I explained to her and she loves loves us and how amazing and helpful we are each time she has needed to contact us. Great and very friendly member here!!!!! :) :) :) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-08-04 14:48:35', '2021-08-04 14:48:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072952008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862244', 'Andrew Racuch', NULL, 'Member''s spouse called in and let us know that she turned 65 on 8/1.  I will send out Member change link for member to fill out then refund.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-08-04 14:33:09', '2021-08-04 14:33:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072980013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862244', 'Andrew Racuch', NULL, 'Regina called saying the cancelled their membership because they are Medicare age.  I don''t see anything showing cancellation.  It looks like she turns 65 this month, but her husband is several years younger.  She wanted to talk to someone about the payment -- did direct trans to Patti Baron.    CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2021-08-04 14:29:51', '2021-08-04 14:33:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072935028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055816155', 'Stephen Longo', NULL, 'Brittney called regarding her children''s wellness visits and wondered if they were covered. I explained that because of the plan that she is on the visits will be an out of pocket expense as well as the immunization for her daughter. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-08-04 14:22:59', '2021-08-04 14:22:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072935023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005116123', 'Ronald Levis', NULL, 'Ronald called regarding a screening colonoscopy and I explained that it is not included in his plan. He also inquired about a prescription, in which I sent him the best discount coupon I could find. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-08-04 13:42:46', '2021-08-04 13:42:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072972008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027885418', 'Carolyn Glah', NULL, '8-4-21 Carolyn is healthy and just did her annual physical and mammogram. Wants to reach out to Redirect for chiropractic visits as well via the app. She''s healthy with no current or recent needs. Bob has a mystery pain on the side of his chest without any diagnosis. They did colonoscopy, endoscopy and no knowledge of what''s causing the pain. They will stay with PDHC while sorting this out. IF and only if they can get a clean bill of health note from Dr at some point in the future they will consider moving to SECURE for cost cut in half even though they lose some of Redirect''s benefits which they can pay for on their own. Dr. Anne Maff is not showing in network. Bob is self employed. If they can move they are also open to paying for wellness on own and choosing CARE+ to be able to see own docs still.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-08-04 13:29:33', '2021-08-04 13:29:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000072935018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675217', 'Andrea Davis', NULL, 'Andrea called in regarding her screening colonoscopy and mammogram. She was looking for someone off of a list of specific providers that her PCP provided her. I could not find the specific mammography center in the PHCS network so I advised her to call the facility and ask if they honor Planstin. Her colonoscopy center is in the PHCS network. I also provided Andrea with an email on how to submit your bills to Zion and how to present your MEC card. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-08-04 11:49:59', '2021-08-04 11:49:59'),
