  ('zcrm_1579374000070105003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063565013', 'Kristi Nelson', NULL, 'Member called in asking for us to call around to facilities in her area for an MRI. When I asked if this is something her doctor recommended, she informed me that she has not consulted with her physician about this issue. I explained that she should start with making an appointment with her healthcare provider so that they may take the appropriate steps to get any tests/imaging done properly. Member kept insisting that this is insurance and it should work just like insurance, I then explained that she is part of a medical cost sharing community and that works differently than traditional health insurance. Member did not want to do any of the leg work that is required with this plan and seems VERY confused about what she actually has with MPB.Health. She also stated that she was never told that she had to meet a $2500 IUA before the sharing would begin. She has had a Welcome Call but I am not sure if she truly understands the definition of medical cost sharing or what her plan entails. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-06-16 12:19:08', '2021-06-16 12:24:39'),
