  ('zcrm_1579374000069550038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066091058', 'Clayton Coulter', NULL, '6-7-21 Hi Allison,

You are correct, most states no longer will penalize you for not having an ACA compliant plan. Only a handful of states require this now.  If you use your local county health departments for screenings and shots then we have a membership called CARE+ that removes the MEC. But, this still gives you access to 24/7/365 telehealth, MPB Concierge Service for help with entire membership, including access to most affordable meds, up to 12 virtual or in-person mental health counseling sessions, discounts on health living options such as massages, yoga, tai chi, chiropractic care, acupuncture, etc. For just your husband at the $1000 IUA level the monthly cost is $215 a month.

If you want access to the high-cost annual wellness visits such as mammogram, colonscopies and childhood immunizations ages 0-16 (with a 6 month wait), we have a membership called DIRECT that was built to pair with your DPC. The monthly cost for this is $245 a month.

If you still want to go straight to Zion without any supporting features and assistance, I will just need a quick note from you letting Zion Health know I''ve helped you as your trusted Advisor throughout this process. This will enable me to assist you moving forward. I will forward it to the proper person at Zion to include me on your account to help you.

Thanks!


Wendy Scipione

MPowering Benefits
National Sales Director
Health & Wealth Strategist
Licensed Accident & Health / Life Insurance Agent / CO-CA-FL
Louisville, CO 80027   
