Hi Wendy,

I hope all is well. I wanted to check in with you about our coverage option with MPB. I have researched Illinois health insurance a little more and recently learned that IL residents are actually no longer required to have MEC insurance and will not be penalized. 

After talking this over with my husband we feel like it may be best to utilize a direct primary care membership in our area, use our county health department for annual screenings/shots and the Zion Health Share DPC option only. 

I appreciate all of your help over the last few months. I understand I have already signed up with MPB, but our coverage has not started yet. I am hopeful we can work out a solution to reverse the setup fee we were charged. I think MPB is a great alternative and have actually told a few of my friends about it! But at this time for our particular situation currently we feel we have found a better setup. 

Thanks again for your assistance and time! I look forward to hearing from you.
Allison Coulter', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-06-07 17:01:20', '2021-06-07 17:01:20'),
