  ('zcrm_1579374000069044013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601365', 'Matt Holstein', NULL, 'Matt called to be reminded of how his preventative care benefits work for his daughter- I sent him the preventative care templates and went over them. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-27 14:49:40', '2021-05-27 14:49:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069034021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069438001', 'Beth Blacker', NULL, '5-27-21 Beth "I am currently on Medicaid and despite them telling me that I can remain on it until COVID restrictions are lifted, I feel like somehow it is going to come back to really bite me in terms of penalties. I have communicated with them repeatedly via phone and email that I have been over the threshold since August 2020 but every month they tell me "don''t worry". I am worried...I have heard too many people tell me that they have gotten hit with big tax bills. They don''t have my 2020 returns on file yet and I didn''t pay quarterly taxes last year or so far this year so I am genuinely concerned.
I don''t know if you have any insight re: this matter but wanted to let you know. 
 I just ran a quick report for this year to date and while my gross business income is at around $50K so far, I have business expenses of about $24K. I anticipate the proportion of expenses to income to go down the second half of the year for what that is worth to figuring things out but I am definitely on track to get to at least over $100K gross income by year end but probably closer to $125-140K. Even if my expenses continue to track at about 50% (I expense my car, insurance, phone and a lot of other things through my business obviously) I will still be over the threshold to get any healthcare credits. If it ends up I make significantly less I assume we can reevaluate at the end of the year?" 
She has health issues that she needs to see doctor for right away. Doesn''t want to be limited by Medicaid''s network. Wants best care. Looking at traditional options. Medicaid won''t allow her to be removed from Medicaid until the emergency health crisis is lifted. But, possibly they will now since we''re in level Clear. She''s calling them now to see if they will remove her since her income is way over the threshold for Medicaid. She''ll call me back today or tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-27 14:41:00', '2021-05-27 14:46:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069044008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058247082', 'Anne-Marie Marron', NULL, 'Welcome call complete!  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-27 14:37:43', '2021-05-27 14:37:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000068996028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065246185', 'Matthew Johnson', NULL, 'Zac Emailed me and told me that this member could not afford the plan I will cancel eff 6/1', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-27 14:22:36', '2021-05-27 14:22:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000069050003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000167691', 'Catherine Dailey', NULL, 'Catherine called in requesting information on how to submit her bills to Zion. I sent her the Zion needs submission link and instructions. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-05-27 14:05:31', '2021-05-27 14:05:31'),
