  ('zcrm_1579374000069034013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069192234', 'Nathan Love', NULL, '5-27-21 Nate is 42 as of April, wife is 43 and 2 kids, son 7 and daughter 4. He''s an Independent Rep for WWSRA. Currently with LHS but really wants to fund HSA. Also, his mom is an insurance agent for about 15 years and keep encouraging him to join traditional insurance since she''s seen some health share plans not cover well. I told him my experience with LHS vs SECURE membership. Also explained some plans have caps (like $125L, $250K, etc.) at various levels that folks don''t know or know it''s important when they enroll. That gets folks in trouble. Nate also talked with Cami and Suzie to find out their experience and they are very happy with their membership. I looked up Dr. Christopher Carlson and he''s not showing in the search. But, when I went to New West Physicians their site shows they accept MultiPlan and the PHCS network. I started looking up Dr. Margery Maeder, gyn for wife and Dr. Frederick in Lakewood, Ped, but site went down. Have to try again later. We have next appt set for June 1st to complete enrollment for SECURE $1000/$685. 
UPDATE I found Dr. Margaret (Maeder) Amos in the network as well as Dr. Cynthia Fredericks Pediatrician in Wheat Ridge, not Lakewood. Asking him if this is the correct doctor.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-27 13:36:51', '2021-06-01 10:20:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000068996018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068994027', 'Linda Garcia', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-27 13:32:28', '2021-05-27 13:32:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000068996013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752344', 'Judith Anderson (Knizewski)', NULL, 'Member called in to the Concierge on 5/26 saying that she received a bill from Lab Corp from 8/20 that needed to be paid.  There was some question as to when she was effective with Zion so John & G & I dug into it and Member had submitted her Selection on 7/31 after Aug enrollment file had been sent to Zion.  She remained on Sedera until 9/1 when she became effective w/Zion.  So member would have to submit bill to ASi if it is even preventative.  If it isn''t it would be an out-of-pocket  expense.  I email Joan & Debbie with this information who are working on this.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-27 12:22:56', '2021-05-27 12:22:56'),
