Hey Wendy. If he pays his IUA we can keep the need open. We have an itemized statement from the ER for 1232.17 toward which he can pay his $1000 IUA', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 17:19:34', '2021-05-10 17:19:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763189', 'Karen Levine', NULL, '5-10-21 Enrolling in DIRECT. Has membership with Cloud Medical already and doesn''t use it much. She was frustrated with Sedera bc she felt like they were disorganized. OOOPS!!! She chose SECURE bc she barely uses Cloud and we have the telehealth AND all ACA compliant annual wellness immediately, plus it''s cheaper. I was hesitant to encourage her to cancel Cloud but should have suggested it immediately, not afterwards. My mistake. Now poor Patti has to reimburse her for the DIRECT membership $125. My bad! Next time, just tell Patti and she''ll fix it on the back end. So, SECURE $275/$1000 and cancelling Cloud and Sedera.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 17:17:48', '2021-05-10 17:17:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763225', 'David Lung', NULL, '5-10-21 Moving enrollment to tomorrow due to his work project.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 16:15:55', '2021-05-10 16:15:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067726048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011899568', 'Stephanie Yost', NULL, 'helped Stephanie with a script that will help her verify that her doctor is in the PHCS network via email. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-10 16:15:40', '2021-05-10 16:15:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763189', 'Karen Levine', NULL, '5-10-21 Karen left me a vm and I called and spoke with her husband and left vm with her too. Husband is aging into Medicare on May 12st. He thought his membership will end on May 21st. I told him usually Sedera begins and ends on the 1st of the month. He was worried about the 10 days without membership. He will contact Sedera and double check with them now. I can help Karen for moving forward. She wants something other than Sedera.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 15:56:07', '2021-05-10 15:56:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058247082', 'Anne-Marie Marron', NULL, '5-10-21 Inquiry on Slack - Client Anne-Marie Marron wants to drop her DPC which she''s not happy with. She''s on the Connected plan. I assume she can just drop the DPC and pay the higher monthly rate to MPB without disrupting her membership with Zion. Is that correct? Thanks!

Hi Wendy, that is correct.  She would simply move onto the new membership type with the updated rate. We''d just need an enrollment file sent over with this information (termination date of existing membership type, and effective date of new membership type). As long as the effective date of the new membership type is the day after the termination, Zion Health would consider this to be a continuation of membership with no lapses.

Now I''m asking John how to resubmit the enrollment file. Waiting to hear back.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 15:47:00', '2021-05-10 15:47:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763142', 'Leanne Wagner', NULL, '5-10-21 Freedom Health only paid for part of her annual wellness visit and she paid an extra $100 a month for them to only cover part of the annual wellness visit. Tired of Freedom Health. Choosing SECURE $275/$1000.  No drugs, No smoking and barely drinks. Using ACH w/d. Enrolled successfully. Plans to do her mammogram in July and already did pap screening recently and colonoscopy in Aug. 2020. In great health!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 15:19:58', '2021-05-10 15:35:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067726043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065297409', 'Lauri Wakefield', NULL, 'called to cancel.  sent form and tagged Joan. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-10 15:01:24', '2021-05-10 15:01:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067741033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016005073', 'Kenny Yang', NULL, 'Member called in to Concierge asking questions about Pre Ex and the conversion process.  Member did not respond to 3 emails letting him know about conversion because he was taking care of elderly parents as a result he missed out on the Prex he needed.  He told me that Kevin suggested ACA or Medicaid.  I told him I was unfamiliar with Medicaid requirements, but that he should look into that as it seems like it was his only option.  I advised him that I would need cancellation by 20th of the month.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-10 14:47:09', '2021-05-10 14:47:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067714031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066577036', 'John Malloy', NULL, 'Elizabeth called in regarding coverage while travelling abroad. I let her know that as long as the "super bills" are in English when she submits them to Zion Health, they will be covered as long as the $2500 IUA is met. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-05-10 14:25:08', '2021-05-10 14:25:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067726038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061594028', 'Aftan Murphy', NULL, 'Welcome call complete! - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-10 14:25:06', '2021-05-10 14:25:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763104', 'Bryan Lonergan', NULL, '5-10-21 Enrolling now in CARE+. Talked with doctor and determined it''s best to go with CARE+ and pay cash for wellness. He takes one med for potassium level, I think he said. Writing on application. Choosing $175/$2500 for one year to test water on high IUA. Not expecting any issues. Bryan is thrilled enrolling was so easy!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 14:16:46', '2021-05-10 14:16:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067725013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763225', 'David Lung', NULL, 'Moved note to correct client.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-10 14:11:24', '2021-05-10 14:15:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067741028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058247082', 'Anne-Marie Marron', NULL, 'Wendy called in and told me that this member was unhappy with her DPC and wanted to change to the regular Connected Wkst plan.  I said that I was unsure if Zion Would let us change this in midyear.  Wendy to ask them if they would allow this.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-10 13:36:25', '2021-05-10 13:36:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067741023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066645014', 'Pamela Furr', NULL, 'member called into me again to ask my opinion on a couple of issues that she had.  she is a cancer survivor & has issues with herniated discs in her back.  She told me that she has had a flair up of her back issues and at some time might need to have surgery.  Asked how that would be treated.  I read the PreEx entry in the Zion guidelines and she wasn''t very comfortable with that.  I told her for anything tin the 1st year the would order Medical Records  and depending what they said it might not be shared.  She is also a cancer survivor original Breast cancer then Colon cancer.  I explained that we are not the only organization that has PreEx limitation that she would have the wherever she goes.  She asked me what I thought and I advised her to speak with Steve Remmel about this.  I then called steve and told him of my conversation with her and he said that he would speak to her.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-10 13:34:12', '2021-05-10 13:34:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067741018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044650569', 'Connie Giles', NULL, 'Sent out cancellation form for 8/1 cancellation explained when I would need that.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-05-10 13:27:28', '2021-05-10 13:27:28'),
