  ('zcrm_1579374000067658013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067763142', 'Leanne Wagner', NULL, '5-7-21 My post on Slack @Jeff Lee I have a new potential client that is asking about an annual mammogram that will go through Planstin. She has dense breasts and the drs. usually require an additional ultrasound to review to make sure they can see everything clearly. She''s never had an issue. But, I want to make sure, as long as the dr. codes the ultrasound as wellness, that the ultrasound will be at no cost to the member? Can you please confirm or find out from Planstin?

From Dr. Lee on Slack, "...planstin says that if the ultrasound is billed as preventive then they will cover that."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-07 16:56:23', '2021-05-07 16:56:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067647033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063373030', 'Heather Masuen', NULL, 'Called Leah Garcia to explain what we figured out happened with Heather''s issues.  per Joan. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-07 16:54:37', '2021-05-07 16:54:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067647028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015647085', 'Christopher Lopez', NULL, 'Amber called because she is submitting a large medical need to Zion- she reached out to Zion''s member services for support and was told that she has a $5000 IUA- which is incorrect.  So I told her that I would reach out to Zion''s management team and ask them to confirm the CORRECT information, as well as answer any further questions she may have.  She has JUST scheduled ankle surgery for TUESDAY!  so not enough time to contact HCBB about.  I told Amber to expect a call back from Zion. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-07 16:35:14', '2021-05-07 16:35:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067658008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038689003', 'Eric Lemasters', NULL, '5-7-21 Talk with Eric and he''s interested in possibly moving to SECURE to save $100 per month. This will help them fund their HSA more as well by freeing up some money. Eric has high blood pressure and high cholesterol that he''s been taking for several years with no further problems. Next question I asked Dr. Lee via Slack as follows:

@Jeff Lee I have a potentially new client who visited the ER in March for a twinge in chest area that happened while shoveling 4 feet of snow. He went to the ER to be certain it wasn''t anything bad. He had his heart checked out with all tests and his heart checked out with a clean bill of health. They determined the pain was simply muscular. We just want to make sure this won''t be considered an issue for pre-x with his heart or anything else.  Thanks!

Jeff Lee  10:58 AM
I can''t say for certain but I seriously doubt this would be considered pre-existing unless he has ongoing related muscular issues.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-07 16:27:40', '2021-05-07 16:27:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067647023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058967156', 'Alexandria Wright', NULL, 'sent welcome call scheduler per Wendy.  Also reached out to CirrusMD''s tech support team asking them to instruct Alexandria on how to add her minor daughter to her account.  Tagged Alexandria and Wendy. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-07 15:46:53', '2021-05-07 15:46:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067658003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058967156', 'Alexandria Wright', NULL, '5-7-21  She tried using the Planstin card at Urgent Care and wanted to cancel her membership. I explained it to her. But, she is happy to do the Welcome Call that she never did. She also wasn''t able to use CirrusMD for her daughter bc they couldn''t find her daughter in the system, only her. So, she was forced to go in person to Urgent Care for a bee sting reaction. Could have been managed through CirrusMD. She also used the Planstin card at the pharmacy. It worked and got the price from $59 to $17. But cash might have been better still for an antibiotic. KC will reach out. We looked at traditional insurance at $50K income but she might earn close to $100K with new skin care line they are launching in a week. They have a huge instagram following and believe it will be a big success. She thinks her membership is expensive until I showed her C4 plans and how crappy they are. She''s getting married in Nov to Curtis and they can add him to keep the cost down as family instead of separately.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-07 15:23:52', '2021-05-07 15:23:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067647018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064705055', 'Douglas Whitney', NULL, 'answered call....call dropped.  Called member back and left a message acknowledging the call and letting the member know that we are happy to answer any questions.  Gave office hours and phone number. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-07 15:20:45', '2021-05-07 15:20:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067640012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017126041', 'Steven Strehlow', NULL, 'Spoke with Julie regarding a recent mammogram she had at Simonmed radiology. She is concerned that it will not be covered since they recently told her that they are not in-network. I directed Julie to call Planstin to confirm this and also provided her with a new in-network radiologist list and Wellness visit instructions via email. - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-05-07 14:41:53', '2021-05-07 14:41:53'),
