  ('zcrm_1579374000067362003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027654206', 'Elizabeth Burlingame', NULL, 'Elizabeth called regarding her plan and forgot that she had cancelled her membership. Gave her the Redirect phone # - JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2021-05-04 07:22:23', '2021-05-04 07:22:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067323038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030219010', 'Lori Kleiman', NULL, '5-3-21 Lori called bc turning 60 in June and price going up to $530 from $350. She loves Redirect now that she''s using the Spruce app. She going to an ENT soon to double check that everything checks out fine. Trying to move appt to before 20th to make sure she''s good to go. If not, she can stay put. She has vertigo and migraines. Treating with diet and Imitrex as needed, no more than 2 mg per month. Sees Dr. Jabeen Fatima and she''s not showing in network. But, Lori remembers the PHCS network from before with her PSDHC, so likely she accepts it too. Lori is self-employed. SECURE for $275/$1000.  She''ll keep me posted as she reviews information and possibly moves appt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-03 18:00:33', '2021-05-03 18:09:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067298094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064746174', 'Tamra Dalle Molle', NULL, 'Tamra called to let me know that her son George was unable to get an invite from CirrusMD because the system couldn''t find his information.  I sent a support email to CirrusMD /Brody/ and John Kach for help.  George is feeling unwell and needs the services asap. I told Tamra that it was after hours for John to help but that I would do the best that I could via CirrusMD and Brody''s support.- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-03 17:38:14', '2021-05-03 17:38:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067323033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110789002', 'Devon Petersen', NULL, '5-3-21 Devon is 30, living in Mexico at the moment but will be back in CO as of June 1st. She''s quitting her job next week and taking a break for 3-5 months. She could qualify for Medicaid but it''s CO specific. She might go that route. She''s likely looking at PT or contract work in the future. She has some joint issues and had several surgeries', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-03 17:29:36', '2021-05-03 17:29:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067323028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067333056', 'Joe Werne', NULL, '5-3-21 Creating record now from last summer. Can''t find his record in here. Chose Kaiser and might get Cobra benefit from employer for lack of hours recently.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-03 16:18:14', '2021-05-03 16:18:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067323023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068994027', 'Linda Garcia', NULL, '5-3-21 Cobra benefit not relevant to Larry bc retiring by choice. 

"What is changing for customers eligible for COBRA?
Under ARP, customers eligible for COBRA because of a reduction in hours or involuntary termination of employment and elect COBRA coverage may be eligible for a full premium subsidy that covers the entire cost of COBRA. This is available for coverage from Apr. 1 until Sep. 30 and subsidized through the employer."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-03 16:08:35', '2021-05-03 16:08:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067298089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063373030', 'Heather Masuen', NULL, 'confirmed with Heather that she get''s her therapy benefits through MPB.Health. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-03 16:07:02', '2021-05-03 16:07:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067323018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068994027', 'Linda Garcia', NULL, '5-3-21 Larry 63 and Linda 63 have work insurance now until end of month. Larry is retiring in a week. Referred by Mike Coy. Linda works PT as an RN and is paid via a W2. They will pull $10K a month from retirement funds/401K and Linda''s earnings $2K = $12K per month, therefore $144 K per year. I need to see what Cobra benefits they''ll get with C4 or what APTC. Presented CARE+ at $500/$1000. They just did all of their annual wellness stuff recently. But, Larry likes to go to internist 1x per year and they know they will have to pay on own and not get reimbursed until find a new issues. Larry has 4 meds, zysol for seasonal allergies, doxicosin for prostate/urination issue, gout and anxiety. They need July 1st start date. If choose Cobra it''s $1700 full cost without ARP.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-05-03 16:04:34', '2021-05-03 16:04:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000067298084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063373030', 'Heather Masuen', NULL, 'member called to ask how her therapy benefits work- I explained and offered to transfer her to MSEAP.  She declined wanting their telephone number instead. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-05-03 15:52:57', '2021-05-03 15:52:57'),
