  ('zcrm_1579374000065333053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065366043', 'Jayne Asatani', NULL, 'Member &amp; Family $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-22 12:07:43', '2021-03-22 12:07:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065373008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025389187', 'Kenna Crampton', NULL, '3-22-21 Kenna joined through our old Sedera landing page - https://sedera.com/mpowering-benefits-landing/. However, Kenna might be pregnant. They have been trying since Nov. and don''t want to wait. So, traditional ins is the only option. Fortunately CO has opened enrollment again. So, we can get her on for April or May 1st start date. Looking at RMHP or Anthem since only options in their area. Kenn is 32 and husband is 30. Kenna is W2 employee working for a community radio station as W2 and William works for Avalanche Ranch W2 and as song writer 1099. Kenna hrs dropped from 40 to 32 hrs to earn $30K this year and William will earn about $10K, so total is $40K and they will get a $657 APTC. William takes a med for anxiety and otherwise no pre-x. They would like to join CARE+ after they have the baby if possible at that point. No it doesn''t make sense. She loves the mental health benefits with CARE+. She doesn''t currently have any doctors she''s tied to. She typically uses Planned Parenthood for her needs. I''m suggesting an Anthem HSA plan for about $169 a month so they can continue to fund their HSA and use that for the maternity needs. She has about $500 in that account already. Otherwise they can''t afford the higher cost plans with the lowest ded and mop. We will revisit this on Friday at 2:00.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-22 11:56:35', '2021-03-22 12:02:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065333048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059061051', 'Brett Combs', NULL, '4/21 payment declined 1st notice sent-3/22 2nd notice sent - 3/24 3/25-member submitted ne CC info I updated &amp; reran', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-22 11:06:57', '2021-03-25 07:21:12'),
