  ('zcrm_1579374000065146031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065281009', 'Chris Haertling', NULL, '3-16-21 Chris just turned 63 last week. Lives in GJ, CO.  She is "Sick of Obamacare. She''s not able to live the American dream." She''s tired of worrying about how much income she will or will not make. He new accountant Sandy referred her to me and mentioned Sedera. Although Sandy said she''s paying $120 a month! I don''t believe that''s possible. Chris is healthy, single, self-employed running dog grooming business. No meds, no tobacco. She has a DPC membership with Appleton Clinics in GJ. She only used them twice for UTI and something else she couldn''t remember.  When I mentioned the MAP program she shared that she lost her daughter last year and she''s grieving. She sough out a therapist who asked if she was able to eat and drink. When the answer was Yes, they therapist told her she''s fine. She may really appreciate this service! She''s also interested in the Elder Care assistance for planning her own future. She used to pay $184 with large APTC then earned too much and now pays $660. She has gone without insurance previously when cost was $1200 for just her! She was thrilled when the tax credit was removed. She''s interested in DIRECT for $245/$1000. I forgot to mention colonoscopy and mammo included! She knows of deadline but isn''t concerned if she misses a month without anything.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-16 12:40:31', '2021-03-16 13:42:48'),
