  ('zcrm_1579374000065136053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060779416', 'Christine Heinritz', NULL, 'Christine called for help in getting into her MPB.Health portal.  I helped her get into her account- I also explained the other portals on the site.  I recommended a welcome call and sent her an online scheduler as well- I told her that it would be very informative, and very helpful in helping her feel "grounded" in the plan. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-15 16:56:25', '2021-03-15 16:56:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065146018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019362080', 'David Kimble', NULL, '3-15-21 "Hi Wendy,

Your comment about finding doctors was prescient -- we immediately ran into issues with it.

As a result, I moved to ACA, where the tax credits make the premiums very reasonable (about 1/3 of MPB).

Thanks for all of your help through the years,

Dave"

"Hi Dave,

I''m sorry about your frustrations and challenges! I wish the universities would cooperate. They got increasingly difficult forcing students onto their high cost plans. It''s brutal. Since you qualify for Medicaid then it will take financial pressure off of you. You will just have to make sure you find doctors that accept Medicaid patients.

Here''s the link to cancel your membership - https://mpb.health/member-updates/. Scroll towards the bottom and select "I would like to cancel my membership." Complete the form, sign and submit it."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-15 15:23:24', '2021-03-15 15:23:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065146013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064410541', 'Lori Streim', NULL, '3-15-21 David is considering moving both of them to DIRECT or just him to help deal with his tinnitus. He LOVES Dr. Clint Flanagan who was his Dr. a while back. He is calling Nextera tomorrow and will see if he can become a patient of Dr. Flanagan again. If so, he will join. He''s pondering moving Ilyse to that membership too in order to keep it consistent. Then we need to cancel his Anthem plan which he''s paying $673.87 now with $1234.33 APTC. Without Ilyse on plan for Anthem his APTC is $429 and his cost is $548.61. Therefore, doesn''t really make sense for them. So, really liking the idea of Nextera plus DIRECT $455/$1000 plus $178 = $633 a month! Win-win all around. He''ll call me tomorrow or Wed to finalize plan.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-15 15:18:17', '2021-03-15 15:18:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065136048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032516085', 'Harold Workman', NULL, 'Harold called for information regarding his preventative care benefits.....I went over everything, sent the two preventative care templates.  PLUS I sent him some information about directlabs.com just in case his blood work isn''t STRICTLY preventative. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-15 15:16:24', '2021-03-15 15:16:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065136043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104128', 'Lindsay Tollefson', NULL, '03.15.21:  Called Lindsay - l/m to c/b.  Said I was informed she enrolled on her own.  Asked her to confirm this with me.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2021-03-15 15:06:24', '2021-03-15 15:06:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065136038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065297409', 'Lauri Wakefield', NULL, '03.15.21:  Called Lauri.  She wants to enroll later this week - by Friday.  Said she''d be fine doing it herself.  I told her to call me if she runs into any issues or has questions.  Asked her to let me know when she has enrolled.  She said she is going to choose a $2500 I.U.A.  instead of $1000.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2021-03-15 15:03:03', '2021-03-15 15:03:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065146008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065246029', 'Martha Johnson', NULL, '3-15-21 Richard Bondareff is looking at this for his 57 year old wife Martha Johnson. Richard is 65+. Martha is healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. She''s retired and sells pottery on occasion but is otherwise retired. But, they are looking at local DPC in Asheville for $99 a month paired with DIRECT for $245/$1000. She''s already had her colonoscopy and won''t need another until Medicare age. They are moving from FL to NC for April 1st. They were referred by Jaime Boswell to Sedera. I told him that Sedera has newly age banded rates which aren''t ideal for the older members. I said they are great but we aren''t offering them anymore.  He was impressed and will get back to me before the deadline this week to possibly enroll for April 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-15 14:43:10', '2021-03-17 10:49:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065136033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044842382', 'Amy Tuttle', NULL, 'Robert Amy''s husband called in and said that they very confused on what they have here. He asked what they are paying us for and who I am. I broke everything down for him on who we are, who Redirect is, and and Sedera is. He was reading and email that was sent to him from their Advisor Jill Clark. The email states that for any help with finding providers and anything along those lines they are to call MPowering Benefits first and we can help them do that. Which is wrong. Amy & Robert have Redirect and Redirect are the ones that are supposed to help them with anything medical going on and making appointments and finding providers. Not us. Robert then started reading about when they need to make a medical Need after going over their IUA amount. I said yes that will be with Sedera. I explained how that works and what Sedera will do by helping them with the medical cost''s AFTER Amy has paid out of pocket their IUA they are to contact Sedera and open up a Need. Gave him all phone numbers he needed and made him feel a LOT better about what to do. Not as confused anymore. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-15 14:01:01', '2021-03-15 14:01:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065132089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104296', 'Roland Jefferson Jr', NULL, 'Member &amp; Family $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-15 13:52:15', '2021-03-15 13:52:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065132084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019362080', 'David Kimble', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request I will process &amp; cancel billing', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-15 13:40:06', '2021-03-15 13:40:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065136028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044842382', 'Amy Tuttle', NULL, 'Amy called in and said that she is sick with her thyroid and she needs to see an endocrinologist and can not find any around her and if I can help her with that. I let her know that for that type of situation she doesn''t need to stay in a network per say and go to anyone she would like. She is to pay for that out of pocket up to her IUA. Anything more she would need to contact Sedera. She was shocked to hear this and said "Well what do you guys pay for then? Isn''t this insurance?" I said no its not and she asked what this was then. I told her it is Medical Cost Sharing. I then told her that she needs to contact Redirect and they will help her with making appointments and if it meets their requirements of preventative they will pay for it. Provided her with Redirect''s phone number. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-15 13:39:48', '2021-03-15 13:39:48'),
