  ('zcrm_1579374000065015013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065014070', 'Mong-Tuyen Nguyen', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-12 10:13:23', '2021-03-12 10:13:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065015008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065014057', 'Tyna Pearson', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-12 10:06:02', '2021-03-12 10:06:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065013008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529495', 'Keith Purcell', NULL, 'Susan called in and had a few questions. First she said her husband Keith has to go in for surgery on his eye and she said she is pretty sure it will be over her IUA and when she is trying to log into the Sedera app to start a Need it has the wrong phone number which is their old landline, it says to change anything to send a text to the number but its not a cell phone number to text. I said she would need to contact Sedera to fix that and regardless I would suggest for her to call them about Keith''s surgery because there is a process he needs to go through when it comes to surgeries. Second she said she doesn''t know if it is already too late but back in Oct or Nov she has annual blood work done and was not thinking and just handed them her credit card to pay because she usually is a self pay out of her HSA for her blood work for her thyroid checkup. So she asked if it is too late to possibly get reimbursed for that. I told her that she would need to contact RCI about that as they are they ones that deal with her Preventative portion of her plan and provided her both RCI''s phone numbers along with Sedera''s for the first 2 issues. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-12 10:03:37', '2021-03-12 10:03:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065015003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065014004', 'Carrie Ballas', NULL, 'Member Only $100 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-12 09:55:26', '2021-03-12 09:55:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065013003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027741134', 'Susan Nadeau', NULL, 'Susan called in and asked if it is us or APEX that she needs to speak to about her 1095-B form having incorrect information on there. I put her back to Patti because I know Patti can look into the APEX/RCI Portal and see all the info. She took care of it and let the member know that she does not need to file this form and it is only for her records. As there is no individual mandate anymore to show proof of coverage, which is what the 1095-B form is for. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-12 09:20:52', '2021-03-12 09:20:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065012003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061665001', 'Mike Swanson', NULL, 'Referred him back to his upline advisor Steve Remmel with further questions about pricing etc. as per Joan. Vanessa  Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2021-03-12 08:18:23', '2021-03-12 08:18:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065009003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064545034', 'Tim Tolman', NULL, 'Member decided that this plan would not fit his needs.  So he submitted cancellation request.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-12 07:55:08', '2021-03-12 07:55:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104048', 'Lori Goldman', NULL, '3-11-21 Lori 43 is self-employed with LLC and does mental health counseling. Moving to Boulder by April 1st but in MA now. Will use Mitch Magdovitz''s mailing address until she knows her new address. She prefers functional medicine doctors and understands she will have to pay self-pay for anything that she''s already seen a doctor for or had symptoms. Most of her health issues are from long ago. However, she did have basal cell skin cancer many years ago, but had a bump in the last year that was tested and turned out benign, plus moles removed, etc. I told her to be careful in case he doctor has her entire body on watch as potential for pre-x. Also fell on elbow in Bali but that seems to be healed. Lived in Amsterdam as well. Looked at Kaiser HSA for $414.95 and $330+ on marketplace. Understands trad doesn''t honor alternative medicine, so it''s not ideal. The HSA is super important to her. She will read it over and decide tomorrow and call me.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 17:57:59', '2021-03-11 17:57:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061924134', 'Kristen Lassalette', NULL, '3-11-21 Kristen is struggling with getting her provider to accept the PHCS network saying that they are not or no longer in network. Dr. Brooke Halliwell is showing up in the search and so is Teresa Hall! She''s going to call Planstin tomorrow to get their assistance. She cancelled her appt for tomorrow to try to handle this. She will decide if she wants to keep membership or change it since she can''t get this covered. She also doesn''t want to change doctors since her dr. has managed he thyroid issue for many years. She will keep me posted as to what she learns. She was very appreciative for my help and Michele''s from earlier.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 17:47:57', '2021-03-11 17:47:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104184', '(Ronald) Shaefer Welch', NULL, '3-10-21 "Our due date is May 9th but will likely be more like the end of April with twins.

We are currently covered through my work. My work pays my premium and then we pay $525 per month for Shaefer which we really can''t afford. Adding on twins to that plan would be an additional $750 per month, so we''d be looking at upwards of $1,200 per month for just the three of them.

We are currently trying to get Shaefer off of my work''s insurance plan and onto something more like a community medical cost sharing plan, but it''s looking like we have to have a "qualifying reason" to get him off my work''s plan and a non-insurance plan does not qualify. So we may be stuck with him on my work''s insurance until the end of the year. "

"Ok great. I Actually just had a meeting with our HR gal at work and did acknowledge that having the twins will qualify as a reason to take Shaefer off my work''s insurance. She also did a ton of digging with our insurance rep and says we can get him off sooner too if I say he will be immediately enrolled in another plan."

Ali will stay on work insurance. They are paying for hers. Once she has the babies, if it goes smoothly, she will add them to Shaefer''s membership. If there are complications they will likely wait until those are resolved on her current ins. Shaefer is an independent contractor with multiple jobs such as musician, fishing guide, works for ski company and is a private chef! Looking into SECURE for him first at $275/$1000. She goes to Valley View in Glenwood but I''m not sure that''s in the PHCS network. I gave her the name of PHCS to ask when they are ready to find a pediatrician if they add the twins. They will likely have Shaefer join for April 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 17:29:05', '2021-03-11 17:29:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004637027', 'Beverly Kotowich', NULL, 'Beverly called to cancel, I sent her an online cancellation form and tagged Jane in it. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 16:17:36', '2021-03-11 16:17:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065014004', 'Carrie Ballas', NULL, '3-11-21 Carrie, Tyna Pearson and Mong-Tuyen Nguyen AKA - Dannie enrolled in SECURE $1000/$275 EO for each. They may add family members later. Carrie may also share it with her patients once they test the waters and like it. Tyna''s has a wife with pre-x who will be joining traditional insurance. She was curious about if it''s a conflict to have traditional insurance and MCS. I told her MCS will be considered as the secondary insurance in that case.  They are all super nice and excited about this. Carrie is paying the entire cost for all 3 of them!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 16:07:30', '2021-03-11 16:09:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063644001', 'Carlos Galvin', NULL, 'requested membership cards from Zion/Planstin per members request. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 15:33:55', '2021-03-11 15:33:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004833045', 'John Mendocha', NULL, 'John called to ask about his welcome materials.....I explained that he hadn''t had a welcome call yet, and that it was important that he schedules one asap so that we can go over his plan and then send him the post welcome call email summary so that he has a better understanding of his plan.   He also told me that he wasn''t set up with CirrusMD yet.....so I tried sending him an invite but couldn''t find his information in Cirrus'' system so I emailed their tech support for help.  Also John told me that he never received his membership cards from Zion health.....so I told him that I would reach out to Zion and ask that they send them asap. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 14:51:58', '2021-03-11 14:51:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005271339', 'Christina KUB', NULL, '3-11-21 Chris chose an Anthem plan on exchange. I left her a vm to call me to chat about some new options. I will send her an email as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 14:32:59', '2021-03-11 14:32:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065003003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001175486', 'Katharine (Katie) Armstrong', NULL, '3-11-21 I sent her an email outlining all of the benefits she had with her HES membership. Patti and I talked and she backdated her cancellation to 3/1/21.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-11 14:26:14', '2021-03-11 14:26:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064993023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046483021', 'Rochelle Kirkwood', NULL, 'Rochelle called again today and said that she never got the email I sent about looking up Providers in the network. I told her I did send it but while on the phone I''ll send it again. She got it and was looking through it but I ended up looking up a provider and facility for her on the phone. Both I looked up are in the network so she is all set for her appointments. She thought that when she goes to them presents her RCI card AND then pays out of pocket. I said no no no you never ever pay out of pocket for anything Preventative. That is the whole point of giving them the RCI card and staying in the network. The billing will go through RCI as the billing address is on the back of the card and phone number for the front desk to verify benefits. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-11 14:21:24', '2021-03-11 14:21:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062869009', 'Al Parsano', NULL, 'sent welcome call scheduler link to Johanna. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 13:33:40', '2021-03-11 13:33:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571414', 'Donald Henig', NULL, 'called Donald and left a message, I told him that I would be able to answer all of his questions that he sent to info@ last night....I told him that his questions are so BROAD in scope that he would need to call and have an actual conversation about them.  I told him that he does not need to schedule a welcome call to have these questions answered. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 13:18:08', '2021-03-11 13:18:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000065000003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062264001', 'James Sewell', NULL, 'James called in again and told me that he hadn''t heard back from either John or Patti about the favor that he had asked of them- getting him onto CirrusMD immediately.  I spoke with Patti- she told me that she would talk to John about this after he is out of his meeting that he is in. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-11 13:00:34', '2021-03-11 13:00:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064993018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061665001', 'Mike Swanson', NULL, 'Mike and his wife Lea called in and asked for me to look up and compare/negotiate pricing for Preventative lab work that Lea needs to get done from her Annual Wellness visit with pricing they have. I told her that the only things that we look up pricing for in your area are bigger procedures like certain MRI''s, X-Ray''s, Ultrasound''s, etc.. For blood work, especially preventative blood work HCBB doesn''t have that in their system as something to look up and we don''t have any other services to use for that. We especially do NOT negotiate ANYTHING. This is something that members keep thinking we do and we don''t. We are not medical professionals to be able to do that. I did however tell them that I can email them information about a discount lab work website they can use to look up the tests needed and they will be given information on those tests at discounted rates. They were perfectly happy with that that is was at least something I was able to give them and not nothing. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-11 12:46:00', '2021-03-11 12:46:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064976068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061665001', 'Mike Swanson', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2021-03-11 11:49:08', '2021-03-11 11:49:08'),
