  ('zcrm_1579374000064870008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064873014', 'Donna Fedor', NULL, 'Member &amp; Spouse  $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-09 13:07:35', '2021-03-09 13:07:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064870003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005998017', 'Madeline Grieder', NULL, 'Member Has cancelled w/Liberty.  I sent her the cancellation Link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-09 12:49:55', '2021-03-09 12:49:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027529151', 'Sherry Marriner', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation as she enrolled with Zion.  I will cancel Sedera (via outlook) &amp; RCI and billing .', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-09 11:58:29', '2021-03-09 11:58:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064738046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779377', 'Jack Bowlin', NULL, 'Jack called in and said that he wanted to go have an annual physical because he has had some issues going on with his stomach among other things that have not been normal. I told him that if he goes in and has his physical for injury/illness related issues that is not something that is going to be covered or considered preventative anymore. That goes into the realm of Diagnostic. He understood after I explained why. So he asked some questions on how to go about getting tests done and blood work. I told him that he needs to start with his primary doctor and explain to him what is going on and what exactly he wants to have looked at and tested. His doctor will then either do the lab work in house or write out a script for Jack to take to a lab and get done. I suggested that he contact Zion to let them know about this and that they will be able to help him with what to do next after he meets his IUA. He told me that he also sent in a claim with Zion already from an incident that happened over Christmas time and that he with the one hospital visit paid his IUA but has not heard anything back yet from Zion. I told him to definitely give them a call and ask about his Need along with these issues that is he is having now. He is thinking that everything could be all related and if that is the case we want to make sure he does not overpay another $1000 when he didn''t need to is this is all going to be 1 need. I recommended that he wait until he gets these health issues figured out to have his Annual Wellness Visit because we don''t want that preventative visit that should be covered at 100% turn into a diagnostic visit and then he pay out of pocket when he shouldn''t have to. He is all set with emails I sent and is starting on getting in contact with Zion and getting tests done to figure out what is wrong. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-09 11:17:14', '2021-03-09 11:17:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064836003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027529151', 'Sherry Marriner', NULL, '3-9-21 I was informed by Rod that Sherry is aging up to 60-64 with Sedera and price is increasing significantly. He agreed I should reach out to her.  Sherry has no pre-x, no issues. Most recent problem was 5 years ago with vertigo that was resolved. Sherry is local and couldn''t remember who referred her originally. She thinks it was an insurance guy in Boulder that sent her.  She''s an independent travel consultant. Biz has halted bc of covid. But, she''s still registered with the company she works for and is 1099 contract worker, pays her annual fees, etc. She''s nervous that without enough production they''ll end her contract this year. But, she''s hoping to get business soon of course! Told her if loses her income source we can move her to Care+ if necessary. But, she''s thrilled about SECURE $1000/$275. She''s super healthy and prefers alternative care as well. Also never understood how HSA''s worked. She will ask for information from Concierge to gain help setting one up. April 1st start date.  She also completed cancellation form for PSDHC. She set up ACH payment with new membership. She won''t be home for a week. She will then upload her proof of self employment at that time. All set and super happy!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-09 10:37:59', '2021-03-09 11:01:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064829602', 'Malik Irby', NULL, 'Member &amp; Spouse  $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-09 10:11:00', '2021-03-09 10:11:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064738041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048462261', 'Brian Tilley', NULL, 'Brian called and said he received his 1095-B from Apex/RCI and said his social security number was wrong. I told him that he would need to contact RCI about that but then he asked if it was possible that his social was wrong on our end that RCI got from us. I put him through to Patti to verify this. She said it was correct in the CRM but in the RCI Portal it was wrong. She fixed it. But I let Brian know that he does not need that from to file his taxes as there is no Individual Mandate anymore requiring proof of insurance, which is what that form is for. It is just for his personal records and the IRS actually themselves says to not file that form. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-09 09:52:55', '2021-03-09 09:52:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064833003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000009850101', 'Elizabeth Spano', NULL, 'sent new welcome call scheduler per Wendy. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-03-09 09:22:44', '2021-03-09 09:22:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059061180', 'William Reyes', NULL, 'Member called in again had not been billed for 3/21.  Billing date had been entered wrong corrected this and billing should be correct now.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-09 08:46:57', '2021-03-09 08:46:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064738036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060921278', 'Timothy Dilley', NULL, 'Tim called and said he got his Welcome Package in the mail with the QR card and asked if it was really sent from us. I said yes and explained what the QR card is and how it works. He then asked if on the website that the QR code brings him to has a privacy policy that he can read because when he clicked something there was nothing there to read. I told him we do not have anything to do with Qr Life Code''s website. We do not run it or anything along those lines. I said that is not our website and is a separate company from us. He completely understood and said that is no problem and will contact them and figure it out. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-09 07:59:13', '2021-03-09 07:59:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064738031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091788', 'Ben Sargent', NULL, 'Member called 3/9/21 concerning or wanting directions on how to find a lab in network for blood work.  DP', 'debbie pasqualucci debbie pasqualucci', 'debbie pasqualucci debbie pasqualucci', '2021-03-09 07:46:57', '2021-03-09 07:46:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165388', 'Kimberly Baldwin', NULL, '3-8-21 Kimberly cancelled her colonoscopy appt scheduled at Boulder Medical Center bc the cash price after a 30% discount was still $4600! Insane. I''m having KC help her find a better place. It''s for her first ever one as part of annual wellness bc 50 years old.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-08 20:40:43', '2021-03-08 20:40:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027654432', 'Sarah Mandell', NULL, '3-8-21 Sarah called to understand her membership more and to mention she''s referring Connie Bruce and some others. Told her to do so via 3-way email. She''s been to chiro and dental check ups and that''s it. She won''t use virtual healthcare. She''s mostly eastern medicine person. She''s never taken flu vaccine and will never take covid vaccine. She tried to review VAERS site but had trouble, same as me. Doesn''t do her annual wellness visits, so CARE+ is best. She''s is private chef/self-employed. But, paying $340 now and can pay $215/$1000 if she switches. She wants the Vaccine Bill of Rights email as well! Super happy to talk with someone who''s like-minded she said. It''s a balance of speaking up and also not creating strife amongst friends and acquaintances.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-08 17:33:21', '2021-03-08 17:33:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005454035', 'William Valentine', NULL, '3-8-21 Spoke with William twice today about their financial issues. Going from $700-$800 for health ins up to $1361 is going to crush them and removing kids so kids have to pay on their own. Spoke with Lily today to help her. Sharon earns about $40K in W2 employment. William will make about $45K minus expenses which he guesses he could then make $20K-$40K depending on many variables. His biz is in audio/visual for restaurants which is belly up now bc of covid. So, went into construction work to stay afloat and got lucky with a big contract last year to earn $40K but that only happens once. They now have a $16K in tax debt due to not updating their income and collecting APTC for the year when they earned too much and their income was well above the threshold with the kids income as well.  They worked out an $800 month payment for that with IRS. They now have a $25K Home Depot cc debt for work with 2 yr no interest, but then jumps to 29% interest for the entire amount if it''s not paid off by then.  He calculated that could be about $15K. They have about $10K-$20K medical debt with ER visit this year. Car debt is about $6K-$10K and mortgage is paid via a HELOC. It was interest only at $500 month and now went up to $1500-$1700 month! William has epilepsy. Seizures stopped for past 5 years due to taking cannabis and trilpten (SP?). BUT, cannabis costs about $300 month since not allowed to grow more than 12 plants on own and he needs more to live. Disease began when he was 14. MCS not a good option. Also Sharon had breast cancer in about 2018 or so and is still being monitored ongoing. They do have $16K-$18K in bank at least to help with all of this. Working on Debt solution with Gary Lowe and Pivotal Wealth Team.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-08 16:36:01', '2021-03-08 16:36:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064775008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165388', 'Kimberly Baldwin', NULL, '3-8-21 Sent her an email and left vm to instruct her about mammogram that is now a diagnostic one, not wellness per KC''s instructions.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-03-08 15:27:00', '2021-03-08 15:27:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064768033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061522018', 'Boyd Newsome', NULL, 'Boyd called in and asked about what the 2 cards are that he got from us, his QR Life Cards one for him and the other for his wife. I explained exactly what the cards are and what he needs to do to set them up. That is all he needed. All Set. -Kf', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-08 14:55:34', '2021-03-08 14:55:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064768028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001637159', 'Gretchen Wegner', NULL, 'Gretchen called in and had a bunch of questions as she is very overwhelmed with all the different components to this plan but is very much wanting and willing to learn everything so much so that she has a 5 page word document with everything that was talked about on her Welcome Call and any other time she has asked questions. She has all the names, numbers, and so on written down. She used to have Sedera so with her notes a lot of them are from when she was with them so she has just crossed out Sedera and put Zion, etc.. We tried getting her logged into the member portal both me and her while on the phone and it keeps saying invalid credentials, so I am going to get with John to fix that. We talked about CirrusMD and who they are and while on the phone she downloaded the CirrusMD app and registered as well. She then said that a few months ago she had and still has a lot of pain going on with her neck and she was so afraid to call into her because she was so overwhelmed and just wanted to go to the doctor and take care of it so she has been paying out of her HSA. So she asked what she needs to do now because it seems this issue is becoming a lot more complex and she needs to keep going to doctors about this. She thought she would need to get a 2nd opinion with everything like it was with Sedera. I told her no that she actually has been doing the correct thing by paying out of pocket for now and that she is only to pay up to her IUA of $1000, after that she is to contact Zion and start the Need process which I told her all she needs to do is call Zion and they will walk her through the whole process. I sent her the email as well stating what she needs to do and Zion''s contact info as well like she asked for. She said she will definitely be calling to just get everything straight with all of her notes just so she is comfortable with how all of this works and she said god forbid something happens to her and her parents know what to do in that case. She asked if when she is done with organizing her notes if she could send the word doc into me and I could look it over for her and tell her if there is anything written down wrong, etc. I said of course I would be more than happy to and this is amazing that she is so into the plan and wanting to make sure everything she does is correct. Will email her about the outcome of her getting into the Member Portal once I get with John. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2021-03-08 14:02:27', '2021-03-08 14:02:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064766078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055920115', 'Peter Jonas', NULL, 'Parent Deborah called in and told me she had to update CC on file I will send out link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2021-03-08 14:01:04', '2021-03-08 14:01:04'),
