  ('zcrm_1579374000064284016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065676004', 'Jonathan Pratt', NULL, '2-24-21 Jonathan is 64 turning 65 10/4/56 in 80301. He getting divorced and it''s finalizing next week or so. He has been getting ins through his wife''s employer but that will end. He''s retired now and income is from investments. He exercises and does not smoke. He has seem mental health drs. This past year had a number of health issue with urological procedure and enlarged prostate, blood in urine. Therefore, MCS is not a good idea. We''re looking at ACA, either lowest cost Friday Health $609, or HSA which has many options around $750 or Bright Health $0 ded for $770. He''s not tied to a doctor. He did learn of GoodRX and was seeing his generic meds for cheaper. He will look into using that moving forward. He''s also starting to understand the value of self-pay vs ins. He will contact his wife to see if he can remain on their Kaiser plan until the end of March.  Will call me when has clearer idea of what he wants to choose for April 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-24 13:46:38', '2021-02-24 13:46:38'),
