  ('zcrm_1579374000064230047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '2-23-21 Jillian was referred by Alicia Turbidy who really likes her membership. Alicia is still with Sedera since had a health issue. I explained to Jillian that Alicia''s exact membership is no longer offered. However our SECURE membership is best suited for her now. She and husband are both self-employed but he''s more the bread winner. They are healthy, no meds except 19 year old son on Zoloft for OCD. Somehow he was accepted to Medicaid since Freedom Life rejected him. He''s still their dependent, so I don''t know how he qualified. She''s nervous about it. She might just add him to this to be safe. One kid is off to school with school insurance. So, 4 will likely join SECURE $1000/$685. Paying $1500 now and don''t even get preventative. She was asking if she can get bone density test through preventative. I told her I wasn''t sure. She should ask her doctor. She said in Aspen it costs $1000!  I told her to find out the cash price that they are legally obligated to provide. We will talk again on Thursday to enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-23 18:04:17', '2021-02-23 18:04:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064230042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064410489', 'Michael DePaso', NULL, '2-23-21 "His name is Michael Depaso  his is a doctor and is retiring.  He is in AZ 520-245-8530.  
    he has a Factor 5 deficiency but he only had an issue with it 15 years ago (that sounds genetic to me) BUT he runs all of the tests and everything himself! 62 yrs old, leaning more towards Care Plus." KC
Michael is a family physician and ending on April 31st with current insurance and contract with doctor group as W2. So, CARE+ is best. He also can get his own meds, consultations, psa levels checked, immunizations done all on his own. Really just wants catastrophic and hopes he won''t need the mental health part, but you never know. He wants a May 1st start date which we will have to make note of on Thursday when he enrolls. He hasn''t had any issues with Factor 5 Disorder and his dr. says as long as e keeps taking warfarin med he can live to 100! Appt. next on Thursday Feb. 25th. He had done much research already and MPB and Zion and appreciates that we are both well respected companies in the industry.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-23 17:54:43', '2021-02-23 17:54:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064245013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059427020', 'Doug Lewis', NULL, 'Kelley just called to make sure that she was running her preventative care PHCS network searches correctly!  She is right on track!  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-02-23 17:11:36', '2021-02-23 17:11:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064230037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065038076', 'Willow Aureala', NULL, '2-23-21 Still need to ask who referred her! I forgot. She''s 58, mostly healthy but has hypothyroid issue and chronic insomnia. Takes meds for both. She doesn''t have insurance now and doesn''t want to sign up for ACA. Doesn''t want to support gov, would rather support private companies and DPC. Member of local DPC. Worried about what Biden will do with laws and penalties. But, she''s a W2 employee as teacher for a university. So, only CARE+ and DIRECT are an option. She''s considering getting a mammogram and colonoscopy per encouragement from her DPC but not sure still. No history or risk in family or anything.  She''s on Big Island in HA and 3 hours behind. I mentioned Whole Health Living with dental discounts but she''s leery that there will be any places locally to gain a discount. I don''t know yet. We are talking again on Thursday to potentially enroll for April 1st start date. Bummed missed deadline for March 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-23 16:00:08', '2021-02-23 16:00:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064230022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065676004', 'Jonathan Pratt', NULL, '2-23-21 Jonathan came to me from Jennika Wildau and we are talking tomorrow at 11:00. He went online and wanted to review the plan options and prices before our call. He submitted his email address and then received an email from Leslie Jablonski saying that she will be his Advisor. He was taken aback and told me! I wasn''t familiar with her name until I looked it up in the CRM. I told him we always like to keep the clients with the Advisor that the referral came from, ie. Jennika. He was relieved and we will proceed with our call as planned.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-23 15:09:58', '2021-02-23 15:09:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064245008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442145', 'Suzanne Picard', NULL, 'SEE TICKET. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-02-23 14:57:33', '2021-02-23 14:57:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000064245003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442145', 'Suzanne Picard', NULL, 'Good afternoon Jami,


This is the latest update on Suzanne Picard, I just spoke with her today.  She will need your help with her Lumpectomy w/ Breast reduction surgery.  She chose Dr. Stephanie Miller to be the oncologist surgeon 303-296-1370 and Dr. Karen Lo as the plastic surgeon 303-830-7200.  She thinks this will be performed at Rose Medical Center, but she is unsure﻿.  She received the results of her genetic testing and a Her2 test- and they both came back negative- she told me that it''s great news because she won''t have to go through any chemo before the surgery now.


