  ('zcrm_1579374000064063003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033185042', 'Lynn Quire', NULL, 'Good afternoon Lynn,

I have just gotten off of the phone with Jennifer Chasteen at RCI/Apex and John over at CitizensRX- they both told me that you are an active member of theirs, and if you are trying to use your benefits at a pharmacy,  that is not Sams Club or Walmart, and the pharmacist is putting through your ID number on the card and it is showing that you are NOT a member of theirs...that information is wrong and that the pharmacist must call CitizensRX directly to confirm your benefits. 

All of that being said....I could not get a guarantee from either of them that the medications would be a covered expense, this is because you have a very basic MEC (minimal essential coverage) plan that only covers the 64+ preventative care services as mandated by the affordable care act,  yes, birth control is one of those covered expenses, but the ACA will only cover it monthly when prescribed as a contraceptive. 

My advice to you would be that you ask your pharmacist to call Citizens RX today, if Citizens RX does not cover the expenses, then you can use the coupons that Kelly has given you to at least cut your expenses. If you have any issues with the coupons that Kelly has given you then you can ask your pharmacist to help you find the correct coupons for their store or download the GoodRX app on your phone to help alleviate any of the confusion that your pharmacist may be experiencing.   If you would like ANOTHER option.  I have reached out to Reid at WorldMedRX for a quote on all of your scripts. 

Tretinoin Cream 0.05% x 40g $85.86
Neuac 1.2% - Unavailable
Yaz 3mg/0.02mg x 84tabs $160.09
Larissia  .1mg/0.02mg x unavailable
Levonor  0.15/30mcg x 90tabs unavailable
Testosterone Cyp - unavailable
Tadalafil 5mg x 90tabs $94.95

If you would like to order these from him, please allow 2 weeks for delivery.    Here is his contact information if you would like to place an order with him:

