  ('zcrm_1579374000063572055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063619031', 'Kevin Williams', NULL, '2-11-21 Kevin is with Ravel Health and is putting together a customizable health care solution with DPC, MCS and alternative care. They currently have 115 providers mostly in the Boulder/Denver area and a few out of state. They are planning to start locally first and likely ready to rollout by next open enrollment in fall 2021. Their model will be subscription based and allow employer groups and employees create their own plan. Employers can pay their chosen amount towards the health care solution post tax in paycheck and encourage employees to put the money towards a healthcare membership. They plan to focus on small businesses under 50 employees initially. They will create a custom link for their employer groups to enroll. They will not collect the payment. However, they will take a 15% cut from the membership monthly fee. If group ONLY chooses DPC they may lose money on that. However, if choose MCS and alternative care then their model works. He''s thinking perhaps if average individual member cost is $250 that means $37.50 in commissions which is split half to ravel and half to broker, therefore, $18.50 monthly to broker.  They are allowing members to choose their own DPC locally, choose between Altrua, Sedera and Zion. Altrua is the only religious one. Then finally choose their alternative care such as chiro, acu, energy healer, trainer, nutritionist, etc. Folks can add and subtract this part on a month to month basis. They plan to have high touch engagement with their groups and individuals. They have Live Chat which currently takes about 1-2 hrs to respond to. 

On separate note, Kevin is considering his options for lyme disease. He pays most out of pocket. He''s working with a doctor in New York who wants to run more tests, the latest is $500. We discussed most will be considered out of network and therefore maybe won''t help. He''s with Sedera right now and just discovered their Chronic Lyme disease clause which he''s super bummed about.  Perhaps I should suggest Shelley''s nutritionist to him and Mike Kehoe.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-11 12:17:20', '2021-02-11 12:22:57'),
