  ('zcrm_1579374000063567038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064974154', 'Erica Rysberg', NULL, '2-10-21 Erica is 42, self-employed, no tobacco. Came via Mara Simoneau and is on Cobra now for $700 through UHC. Has great plan and $25 co-pays dr. visits and $45 co-pay urgent care. Tracy Shulsinger PA accepts only UHC but does NOT show up in network for RMHP/UHC. She may not accept individual plans. I told Erica to ask Tracy first. Also she''s going to see Dr. Lauren Harrington in Denver and she''s in the network for Anthem and Cigna only. Tracy has gut issues, parasites and sibo. Also has Marcon''s infections/sinus infections as well as mold toxicity. She''s detoxing and taking supplements. Finally takes hormone replacements since she was 16. Uses pellet hormones which are about $300 and last 3 months, therefore, costs $1200 annually. Gets hormones tested 3x year. She says the pellets are way better than pills or other solutions.  Takes oral progesterone and one other med as well. We discussed RMHP/UHC Gold for $422.74 or Cigna Gold $463.66. Cigna is closest to what she has now with a $900 ded. Her UHC has $500 ded that is ending March 31st. Therefore wants an April 1st start date. Also discussed SECURE for $275/$1000 but knows she''s responsible for all of her pre-x costs other than if uses virtual health app.  She''s going to research how much doctor visits will cost and labs, blood tests, etc. to help her decide what makes most sense.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-10 16:07:39', '2021-02-10 16:07:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000063567033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064277164', 'Raissa Wilkes', NULL, '2-10-21 Raissa just has an ongoing thyroid treatment and takes meds for it and 2x per year does a blood test to monitor it. They''ve been paying cash for everything they''ve done in the past 2+ years. Nothing has been close to reaching their AUA. They also pay cash for annual wellness visits. So, leaning towards CARE+ but will talk with Matt to decide about HSA if worth doing that.  CARE+ $1000/$395 or SECURE $500/$1000. Knows of 19th deadline.  Both considered self-employed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-02-10 15:54:35', '2021-02-10 15:54:35'),
